    "updated_at": "2017-05-02T14:24:26Z",
    "body": "> Right. In Gecko, those security restrictions affect every navigation, while \"allowed to navigate\" only affects link targeting, really.\r\n\r\nThis adds confusion as I believe \"allowed to navigate\" also affects `<form>` and `windows.open()` (and in the standard \"allowed to navigate\" is invoked as part of the generic navigate algorithm)?\r\n\r\nDo these \"new\" restrictions ever take effect for scenarios other than `location.href` and `location.replace()`? (I guess that's unclear.)",
