    "body": "> This adds confusion as I believe \"allowed to navigate\" also affects <form> and windows.open()\r\n\r\nYes, sure.  But just the named targeting part of it, right?   That's what I meant; I didn't mean it was restricted to `<a>` only.\r\n\r\n> Do these \"new\" restrictions ever take effect for scenarios other than location.href and location.replace()\r\n\r\nI would have to walk through things very carefully.  I _think_ the answer might be \"no\", though.",
